<p>
<b>Attractions:</b>
Few Tourist destinations in the world have the assets of Orlando, Florida.  Disney World, Epcot, Universal Studios, MGM Studios, and Sea World, among other attractions, al lhave helped ccement the Central Florida city's reputation as the palce to go on vacation.
<p>
<h3>The city for magical, memorable vacations.</h3>

Orlando. It's a top choice of travelers of all ages from all over
the world. And once you've been here, it's easy to understand why! The city
comes by its magic naturally nature has blessed us with beautiful countryside
and practically perfect vacation weather all year round.
<p>
Long an agricultural center, Orlando blossomed anew with the opening of Walt
Disney World in 1971. The excitement has grown non-stop ever since. Vacationers
thrill to the fantasy of The Magic Kingdom and the technological wonders of
EPCOT '94. They're captivated by the mysteries of Earth's marine life at Sea
World of Florida and the natural glories of Cypress Gardens. There's the
big-screen magic and back-lot excitement of Universal Studios Florida and
Disney-MGM, old-fashioned fun at Church Street Station, and a continuing
out-of-this-world fascination with Kennedy's Spaceport USA.
<p>
And, for those who prefer to spend their leisure time indulging in less
structured activities, Orlando is equally appealing. The area offers golf on
nearly 100 excellent courses. Tennis, water skiing and croquet abound and, for a
real change, check into hot-air ballooning, horseback riding and uniquely
relaxing motor home tours.
<p>
Vacationers can always enjoy the quiet countryside and pristine lakes, in virgin
hardwood forests or in primeval wetlands. Or you can spend an afternoon fishing
or canoeing on miles of cool, clean rivers. All in all, it is an adventure you
never outgrow!

<h3>Best of Orlando</h3>

Orlando's best known features, our world-class attractions, offer visitors
something really magical...the chance to visit a new world every day! And they're always growing and changing!
<p>
Where else but Orlando can you stand inches from a killer whale, see a feature film in the making, witness the launch of a space shuttle and shake hands with the world's most famous mouse...all in a single week?
<p>
Wander through fantasy of the first order at Walt Disney World's Magic Kingdom and roam the world of science, culture and fun at EPCOT '94. Go behind the big-screen scenes at Universal Studios Florida or Disney-MGM Studios Theme Park. Make friends with whales and dolphins and tremble at the  Terrors of the Deep  at Sea World of Florida. Take in the natural beauty and water ski excitement of Cypress Gardens, then ride the waves and waterspouts at our spectacular water parks.
<p>
Treat yourself to a romantic cruise. Have dinner in the company of kings, queens and jousting knights. Then catch the music, excitement and fun of Church Street Station or Pleasure Island.
<p>
And there's still plenty of magic left like golf on nearly 100 great courses, tons of tennis and racquet sports, fishing, boating and skiing on Orlando's numerous lakes. And don't forget the magic of the Magic. Orlando's NBA teamwith top draft pick Shaquille O'Neal plays a full season schedule at the Orlando Arena!
<p>In Orlando, the places and players are always changing, so each time you visit, it's like a whole new vacation!

<h4>Culture & Entertainment</h4>
Orlando offers a host of cultural and entertainment options throughout the year.
You can enjoy the arts, theater and music, or visit a historical museum. At
night, Orlando can take you dancing  till dawn or strolling in the moonlight
along a quiet lakefront. Laugh it up at a local comedy club or be a part of the
act with a whimsical Karaoke sing-along. Serious music enthusiasts also will
find an impressive selection. Rock  n roll, jazz, country & western   whatever
your preference, Orlando has it.

<h4>Sports</h4>
Orlando is the home of the Orlando Magic, a National Basketball Association team
that began play in 1989. The Orlando Predators of The Arena Football League also
play at the Orlando Arena. For college fans, the University of Central Florida
Knights and Rollins College Tars hold forth with seasonal sports.
